        <headline>Flood Advisory issued September 24 at 12:27PM AST until September 24 at 3:30PM AST by NWS San Juan PR</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Small stream flooding caused by excessive rainfall is
expected.

* WHERE...Ceiba in Puerto Rico...
Fajardo in Puerto Rico...
Southern Luquillo in Puerto Rico...
Naguabo in Puerto Rico...
Southern Rio Grande in Puerto Rico...

* WHEN...Until 330 PM AST.

* IMPACTS...Rises in small streams and normally dry arroyos.
Dangerous flows over low-water crossings. Water over roadways.

* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...
- At 1227 PM AST, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to
thunderstorms. This will cause small stream flooding. Up to 0.5
inches of rain have fallen.
- Additional rainfall amounts of 1 to 2 inches are expected over
the area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.
- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood
</description>
        <instruction>Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood
deaths occur in vehicles.</instruction>
